From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:03:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Document how filenames that aren't valid text behave

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01947MBgCkoERXfoyRGfCmQi
---
 CHANGELOG.md | 3 +++
 README.md    | 2 +-
 emil.1       | 3 +++
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 5765a20..7b8f3e7 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@
 - Fixed `C-q` inserting an invalid byte, after which the buffer could not be
   saved, when a terminal resize interrupted it.
 - The advisory lock's file descriptor is no longer inherited by shell commands.
+- Fixed filenames that aren't valid text reaching rows or the terminal unchanged.
+  Filenames that aren't valid text are displayed with substitutions, and can be opened by exact path. A substituted name in the minibuffer is just text, and doesn't refer to the original file.
+- Fixed invalid UTF-8 from a tags file reaching the `M-.` definitions menu.
 
 ## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-12
 - `emil --help` added.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f1e4138..5c8d654 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@ Selections larger than  74,993 bytes are not sent to the clipboard and a status
 
 ## Internals
 
-Each buffer is an array of logical lines (`erow`) holding raw UTF-8 bytes. Every buffer contains only valid UTF-8; files that fail validation are rejected at load time. Rendering and text layout never modify the buffer.
+Each buffer is an array of logical lines (`erow`) holding raw UTF-8 bytes. Every buffer contains only valid UTF-8; files that fail validation are rejected at load time. Filenames that aren't valid text are displayed with substitutions, and can be opened by exact path. A substituted name in the minibuffer is just text, and doesn't refer to the original file. Rendering and text layout never modify the buffer.
 
 A row's display width is cached on the row and recomputed when the row is edited. The renderer calculates wrap positions only for the rows on screen, not for the whole buffer.
 
diff --git a/emil.1 b/emil.1
index 3335fa8..88a3d6b 100644
--- a/emil.1
+++ b/emil.1
@@ -496,6 +496,9 @@ Files are loaded in their entirety into memory.
 adheres to the Unix convention where lines are delimited by a single linefeed (LF) character and files terminate with a linefeed.
 A file opened without a terminating linefeed gains one when it is loaded.
 Validation at file load and inserting text in the buffer disallow  null bytes (0x00) or malformed UTF-8 sequences.
+.Pp
+Filenames that aren't valid text are displayed with substitutions, and can be opened by exact path.
+A substituted name in the minibuffer is just text, and doesn't refer to the original file.
 .Ss File Persistence
 When saving,
 .Nm
